  "description": "Which model, as a tool-using agent, keeps data where it belongs when the instruction to move it reads as ordinary content and goes through a tool it is allowed to use, and still follows instructions in data when the person delegates to them? 64 synthetic scenarios with a consistent simulated workspace: 40 attacks in five families (identity in a URL, other customers' data in a reply, a lookalike-domain forward, an authority claim against policy, a toolchain change suggested by tool output) and 24 benign mirrors of them. Graded from the tool-call trace.",
